  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a substantive denial that requires an appeal to overturn; resubmission is prohibited by the payer's duplicate claim rules. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and a denial is on the table, requesting a P2P is a valid and often effective next step to challenge the medical necessity and bundling determination before a formal appeal. The previous P2P request likely did not resolve the issue or was not completed, so re-initiating or ensuring the P2P is properly engaged is the logical next action to progress the claim without incurring the cost of a full appeal yet.",
